ell diversified, comprising five distinct strata: herbaceous / creeping, sub-shrub, shrub, tree, and canopy. The Palmares National Forest protects a portion of the “ Cocais Forest ”, with species that are ecologically and culturally representative of the Caatinga and Cerrado, and serves as a valuable testimony to these ecosystems (Brasil 2022). This is the first record of the genus in Brazil outside the Northern region, where Adisianus fuscus and A. maculatus were described from the Amazon Forest biome (Bretfeld 2002).","","text","",""]]},"V5B5T":{"d":[["SD","SD","iso","",""]]},"V5B63":{"d":[["Massachusetts","8927","mrgid","",""]]},"VBPN":{"d":[["","AR","iso","native",""],["","84","tdwg","native",""],["","CLM-OO","tdwg","native",""],["","COS-OO","tdwg","native",""],["","ECU-OO","tdwg","native",""],["","GUA-OO","tdwg","native",""],["","PAN-OO","tdwg","native",""],["Guatemala, Costa Rica, Panama, Colombia, Ecuador, Brazil, Argentina","","text","native",""]]},"VMYZ":{"d":[["TWN","TW","iso","",""]]},"VMZ9":{"d":[["EHM","EHM","tdwg","",""]]},"XSHC":{"d":[["New Caledonian Exclusive Economic Zone","8312","mrgid","",""]]},"Y2HC":{"d":[["D.R.Congo [Zaire]; Rwanda; Burundi; Ethiopia; Kenya; Yemen (N-Inner Yemen)","","text","",""]]},"Y9YK":{"d":[["Agulhas Bank","21806","mrgid","native",""],["South African part of the Indian Ocean","25551","mrgid","native",""]]},"ZXWM":{"d":[["ZA, Limpopo","","text","native",""],["ZA, Mpumalanga","","text","native",""]]}}